\begin{abstract}
We propose a theoretical conjecture — designated GUES (Geometric Unification through Emergent Structure) — that spacetime geometry is not a fundamental substrate but an emergent property of information flow structure. Taking information flow as given, we argue that: (1) geometry emerges from the structure of information flow and would manifest measurable deviations from smooth manifold behavior at information-dense boundaries; (2) the fundamental forces correspond to distinct symmetry configurations within that emergent geometry, suggesting their unification requires identifying the higher-dimensional geometric object of which the Standard Model gauge groups are faces; and (3) black holes function as information-to-geometry transducers whose cumulative geometric output is a candidate mechanism for observed cosmic expansion, distinguishable in principle from vacuum energy. This paper is explicitly labeled E1 — structured speculation with proposed falsification paths. It makes no claim beyond connecting established physics to a coherent alternative framing and identifying what would need to be true, and what would need to be measured, for that framing to advance.
\end{abstract}

