\section{Competing Explanations}

Rigorous inquiry requires explicitly considering alternatives before converging on a preferred framing.

\textbf{GR + $\Lambda$CDM as sufficient:} The null hypothesis. Spacetime geometry is fundamental. The Standard Model forces are irreducibly distinct. Dark energy is vacuum energy. This framework fits existing data well. GUES must identify predictions that differ from $\Lambda$CDM, not merely reframe the same predictions differently.

\textbf{String Theory / M-Theory:} Forces are already unified geometrically via compactified extra dimensions. The higher-dimensional object is already proposed (Calabi-Yau manifolds). Black holes are extensively studied in this context. GUES must specify how it extends or differs from this program, particularly regarding the information-flow substrate.

\textbf{Verlinde Entropic Gravity alone:} Gravity is already emergent from entropy in Verlinde's framework without requiring the other forces to follow. What does GUES add beyond reframing Verlinde with a black hole expansion mechanism? This is the most pointed competing explanation and requires the most explicit response.

