\section{Open Questions and Next Steps}

The following are the minimum open questions that must be addressed for this conjecture to advance from E1 to E2:

\begin{enumerate}
  \item \textbf{Identify $\mathcal{G}$:} What is the specific higher-dimensional geometric object whose cross-sections yield $U(1) \times SU(2) \times SU(3)$?

  \item \textbf{Specify the transduction mechanism:} How exactly does a black hole convert infalling information into structured geometric output distinct from Hawking radiation?

  \item \textbf{Quantify the expansion prediction:} What correlation between black hole density and local expansion rate is predicted, at what scale, measurable with what current or foreseeable instrument?

  \item \textbf{Reproduce GR:} Show explicitly that the information-flow substrate reproduces the Einstein field equations at classical scales without additional assumptions.

  \item \textbf{Distinguish from Verlinde:} Specify what GUES predicts that entropic gravity alone does not.
\end{enumerate}

%-----------------------------------------------------------
\section{Conclusion}

We have presented GUES — a structured conjecture at Evidence Level E1 — proposing that spacetime geometry emerges from information flow structure, that the fundamental forces are symmetry configurations within that geometry, and that black holes function as information-to-geometry transducers whose cumulative output drives cosmic expansion.

This is an educated guess. The acronym is intentional.

The value of this document is not its conclusions — it has none that are proven. The value is the honest structuring of an intuition that connects to established physics at multiple points, the explicit identification of where the gaps are, and the proposed paths by which those gaps could be closed or the conjecture falsified.

The next version of this paper will either specify the mechanism for black hole geometric output or explain why it cannot be specified — and what that means for the conjecture's viability.

